Subject: [PATCH] aurora: report ENOSPC as DATA_FULL with guarded fprintd

The paired fprintd package prevents automatic print deletion for apple-sep.
Expose ENOSPC as DATA_FULL so clients show their existing storage-full text.
Do not guess which store filled: the kernel uses ENOSPC for both the SEP's
three-finger limit and host persistence capacity.

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/aurora/aurora.c b/libfprint/drivers/aurora/aurora.c
index 3cb7509..75ac0df 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/aurora/aurora.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/aurora/aurora.c
@@ -129,9 +129,11 @@ aurora_ioctl (FpiDeviceAurora *self, unsigned long req, void *arg, GError **erro
           break;
 
         case ENOSPC:
-          /* DATA_FULL makes fprintd garbage-collect another device print. */
-          g_set_error_literal (error, FP_DEVICE_ERROR, FP_DEVICE_ERROR_GENERAL,
-                               "SEP fingerprint slots or host store are full; no enrolment was started");
+          /* Requires fprintd's apple-sep no-GC guard: prints absent from the
+           * host database can belong to another OS sharing the SEP.
+           * The kernel currently uses ENOSPC for both capacity limits. */
+          g_set_error_literal (error, FP_DEVICE_ERROR, FP_DEVICE_ERROR_DATA_FULL,
+                               "Fingerprint storage is full (finger limit reached or host store full); remove an enrolled fingerprint before trying again");
           break;
 
         case ENODATA:
